    "turn_text": "Or maybe it's not news to see that the prosecutors going after Hunter Biden worked love in hand shoulder to shoulder with his defense attorneys to try to conceal from the judge the deal they were giving him. It's placed in a document that even the prosecutor himself says in open court to the judge, judge, I've never seen this done before in my life. And yet he had to have done it. So, he was saying, yep, I saw his at my job to the American people to try to get Hunter Biden off and to conceal how many things we were getting him off of or granting him immunity from being prosecuted for. I share that concern. All the media is as blindly loyal to the woke establishment and to this particular administration and to the people that run it, you have to worry about that. But the drip, drip, drip, drip. I'm unhappy with Mr. Barr, the former attorney general, for taking in the 1023, which he claims credit for, and then doing nothing with it, and then going on, I think it was Fox and saying he's disappointed in the current attorney general for doing nothing with it. The only thing I can figure is that Mr. Barr had decided that, eh, you'd never really convict somebody as popular as the current president of this kind of crime. So why should he have his family suffer for being the Trump appointed Attorney General who brought it out? I'm told that the vote in Washington DC went 92% in favor of Biden. So who wants to live in an area where if you stand up and say, you know, that sign is blue, 92% of the people who are, you see every day in your life in the Safeway or wherever are going to look at you as though you are evil personify. So, I think, I think Barr disappointed us. Obviously, the current Attorney General is as corrupt as the rest of them. I mean, I have never seen such staggering corruption in my lifetime, not in the United States. I've never seen it. I'm not sure I've ever seen it in the world, in the third world countries. You know, there it's the accepted standard. We've adopted their rules.",
