    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "I choose to believe it is redressable. I choose to believe not only that, The American people, once they become fully informed, and of course the democracy is dependent upon a fully informed electorate, that they simply will not stand for it. It is something that I think is mystifying and may be God-given, that the American people have a deep, deep, deep belief in fairness and in truth and in justice. And they hate corruption. And I have friends who grew up in parts of the country where corruption is endemic and people accept it. But I don't think that's the majority of the nation. And I was unhappy with The chairman of the government reform and oversight committee when he didn't get the tape recordings of Biden and the younger Biden agreeing to be bribed or articulating the blackmail scheme, whichever way you want to call it. But I would have to say that And that's, by the way, the issue about which I am most upset with Mr. Barr. The 1023, 1024 comes in and it says, hey, there are these tapes. If you're a prosecutor and I spent quite a few years at the Attorney General's office, I was no prosecutor, but I worked on prosecuting issues and I worked closely with prosecutors. And at times I had prosecutors who hadn't tried cases coming to me and say, how do we do this? And I watched them and they would grind away until they got the bad guy. And I have to believe that what is happening now is it's drip, drip, drip. So what the media is doing, they're hiding it. So we can talk about the fact that all of the elements of the crime are there. Breezma wanted the prosecutor gone. They went to Hunter and then they went to Joe and they said we want him gone Hunter says to the government You don't get 20 no you don't get a billion dollars of government US government taxpayer money my money and this listening audience's money You don't get that unless he's fired In exchange, they fire him. That's a complete crime in itself. But then beyond that, he says, oh, by the way, I want a kicker. I want five grand for me and five grand for my family. It's now just coming out slowly and slowly, but surely. And I think it's seeping through the society. What the left maybe needs is to banish individual communication between people who live in Iowa, or Nebraska, or Montana, and people who live in, you know, New Jersey, or Washington, D.C., or the Virginia area, neighboring Washington, D.C., or New York, or Massachusetts.",
